Below is one possible approach to eliminate the extra “leading” that OpenLayers applies by default between wrapped lines.  The idea is to detect when the text contains a newline and – if the user has not explicitly requested another baseline – switch from the OL default baseline (which is mid-line) to a “top” baseline.  That way each line will be drawn immediately below the previous one, with no extra gap.

