With this change, any `new ol.style.Text({ text: 'foo\nbar' })` that does *not* explicitly set a `textBaseline` will render the first line at the top of the canvas and the second line immediately below it, removing the extra gap you were seeing.  If you still need a different baseline overall you can of course pass in your own `textBaseline`.
